Z||000000||Ironhorse||07-10-2000||10:51 PM||||Hello Fieroholics.  I've finally got the motor in the F-15 and boy does it look SHARP! But there's a problem. It's not getting any sparks to the plugs.  I've determined it's one of the few... Coil bad or/and distributor pick up unit, and/or ingition moldules(can't spell the thing under your distributor).  I'm dead broke, I've put in about 1300 dollar for the enigne, sensor, parts, and etc.  I can't afford to guess or play game of buy and try it.  What would you do?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bugsy||07-11-2000||12:35 PM||||hook it up to a code reader...it'll give you a place to start <BR>Kevin||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||07-12-2000||05:29 PM||||Call your favorite local parts stores, and find one that will test ignition modules, coils, etc., for free.  AutoZone claims to offer free testing, I think. Haven't taken them up on it myself - so can't comment on the validity of their tests.<P>Pickup coil and ignition coil can be tested with an ohmmeter.  A procedure for testing the ignition coil appears in the Haynes manual, I believe.  Might be able to look at your friendly part store's copy for free, if they don't offer testing - or if for some reason you don't believe their test(s).<P>Meantime, you might try pulling coil wire out of the distributor center tower, connecting it to a grounded spark plug, and seeing if the spark gets THAT far.         ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ironhorse||07-12-2000||09:53 PM||||StuGood, this morning based on a gut feeling. I pulled the ignition modules and took it to Autozone.  He hooked it up and all the red light lighted up.. DAMN DAMN DAMN, oh well at least it's 35 bucks.. I'm also gonna pick up the dist pick up unit to be safe.  *WHEW* now I gotta come up with 45 bucks||||reg||1
